21:13:21 [buyer] SHOP SELECTION: {"name": "ggari-shop", "reason": "ggari-shop has the fewest warning signs: average 4.0 across 10 reviews with only 1 low rating, and no overcharging or receipt-mismatch reports. Recent reviews say receipts matched the agreed prices and were signed. One review reports a lamp negotiated from 117 to 100, which fits the 105 budget. We have no history with this shop, so that part is unknown, not negative. moss-and-oak was the main alternative because we have 1 clean purchase there (bookshelf at 266, 0 receipt mismatches). But it has 9 of 10 low ratings (average 2.0), and its newest positive review is an owner-authored self-review, which is weak and possibly manipulative. Its other low ratings come from errors; errors don't prove dishonesty, but they do show the shop has been unreliable. lee-sungsoo and chaewoonee were each reported to issue receipts under a different seller name, and lee-sungsoo was also reported to ask for a review in exchange for a deal. Remaining uncertainty: we have not traded with ggari-shop ourselves, and the lamp price within budget comes from one review, not a quote."}
21:13:29 [buyer] SHOP SELECTION: {"name": "corner-store", "reason": "Trust comes first, and corner-store has the strongest verified record: 46 of our own trades, 38 purchases and 0 receipt mismatches over its lifetime. No review reports overcharging or a changed agreed price. Its one 3-star rating describes a no-deal, which is not evidence of dishonesty. 11im (4.7 stars, 0 low ratings, a lamp bought at 102 with a matching receipt) and ggari-shop (4.0 stars, lamp negotiated to 100) look good in reviews, but we have no trades with either to confirm them. Uncertainty: our last corner-store lamp cost 118, above the 105 budget, so a deal within budget is not guaranteed. 11im would be the best fallback."}
